  "lore": {
    "appearance": [
      "Colossal segmented worm, without limbs",
      "Overlapping chitin plates ringed segment by segment",
      "Ringed drill-like head with jaws at the working end",
      "A single small eye on the collar behind the head",
      "Vents along the body that spray its slurry"
    ],
    "behavior": "It bores through sand and substrate, sets its head against a seam, and forces its pressurized slurry in until the rock fractures and the Nightcap drains toward the well.",
    "company": "One worm opens a well by itself. The Barons fielded them by the dozen.",
    "description": "A colossal segmented worm with a ringed, drill-like head and a body that holds a slurry of sand under pressure, the Frackworm was generated on Endessa by the Syndicate's stolen prototype Generator to work the Nightcap wells. It bores down through the glass of the dead sea floor and forces its slurry into the seams at pressure until the rock fractures and the Nightcap pools drain toward the well. Wildcatters who could afford one opened a well in days that a crew of Drilltails took a season to reach, and the Nightcap Barons fielded them by the dozen. Today the Frackworms still work the cavern networks beneath the dunes, fracturing the substrate for the fortune-seekers who kept drilling after the Barons died.",
    "feeding": "It takes its food from the sand and whatever is in it as it bores.",
    "habitat": "The cavern networks beneath Endessa's dunes, down to the dead sea floor. It does not come to the surface.",
    "origin": "Generated by the Syndicate's stolen prototype Generator to open Nightcap wells for the wildcatters and the Nightcap Barons."
  },
